# Nightly Pipeline Revenue Tally — MANDATORY

**Every night before Dee ends the session, NEXUS must present the pipeline revenue tally. No exceptions. Don't wait to be asked — if the conversation is winding down, present it.**

## When to Trigger

- Dee says "goodnight," "going to bed," "logging out," "done for tonight," "we're done," or similar
- The conversation has been productive and is naturally wrapping up
- Dee explicitly asks for the tally

## What to Include

### MANDATORY: Save to PIPELINE_TALLY.md

**Before presenting the tally in chat, WRITE it to `/Users/deedavis/NEXUS BACKEND/PIPELINE_TALLY.md`.**

This file is the source of truth. Future sessions read it at startup. If you only present in chat without saving, the numbers get lost and recalculated inconsistently.

**Format:**
```markdown
# PIPELINE REVENUE TALLY
**Last Updated:** [Date] @ [Time] ET

## TOTAL PIPELINE: $[X]M+ LIFETIME

[Full breakdown by program, bids, MCOs, etc.]
```

### Pipeline Table (Every Active Opportunity)

For EACH active bid/opportunity in `BIDS:RESOURCES/`, present:

| Column | Required |
|---|---|
| Opportunity name + solicitation number | YES |
| Annual revenue estimate | YES |
| DDI annual margin estimate | YES |
| Contract lifetime | YES |
| Lifetime contract value | YES |
| Win probability % | YES |
| Due date | YES |

### Categories

Break the table into sections:
1. **Drug Testing & Occupational Screening**
2. **Genetic Testing / DNA (DePointe DNA)**
3. **Other Active Opportunities** (title services, notary, courier, NEMT, etc.)
4. **Relationship Building / Future Pipeline** (no active solicitation yet)

### Summary Totals

Always end with:

| Metric | Conservative | Target |
|---|---|---|
| Total Annual Revenue (if all won) | $X | $X |
| Total Annual DDI Margin (if all won) | $X | $X |
| Total Lifetime Pipeline Value | $X | $X |
| Risk-Adjusted Annual Revenue | $X | $X |
| Risk-Adjusted Annual Margin | $X | $X |
| Risk-Adjusted Lifetime Value | $X | $X |

### Closing Line

End with a motivational but grounded one-liner. Not cheerleader energy — grounded best friend energy. Remind Dee what she's building.

## Where to Get Numbers

- Revenue analyses in `WORKFLOW_CHECKLIST.md` files inside each bid folder
- If no revenue analysis exists for an opportunity, estimate based on comparable contracts
- Mark estimates clearly with asterisks and notes
- Use DDI's standard margin model (40-55% for drug testing, 50%+ for title/notary, 10-20% for freight/logistics)

## Why This Exists

Dee said it herself: "This brings daily motivation." Seeing the pipeline value every night keeps the momentum going and reminds her why the vendor calls, portal registrations, and late-night emails matter. This is the scoreboard.
